  "id": "infrasound",
  "term": "infrasound",
  "definition": "Infrasound is environmental noise with frequencies below 20 Hz that humans can barely hear. It can come from natural sources such as ocean waves, wind, and volcanic eruptions, and it travels long distances with strong vibratory penetration, making it a notable environmental pollutant and potential public health concern.",
